    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="badge">Fast &middot; Open source &middot; written in Rust</p>
          <h1>A coding agent for your terminal and desktop.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Use the Cook CLI in your terminal or <strong>Let Cook</strong> on Windows, macOS, or
            Ubuntu. Flexible BYOK: use your own API key, or connect through OAuth with Grok,
            ChatGPT, Claude, and more.
          </p>

          <div class="install-options" data-curl-cta>
            <p class="install-label">Cook CLI · macOS and Linux</p>
            <div class="cmd">
              <code>curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | COOK_INSTALL_CLI_ONLY=1 bash</code>
              <button
                class="copy-btn"
                type="button"
                data-copy
                data-copy-label="Cook CLI install command"
                data-copy-text="curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | COOK_INSTALL_CLI_ONLY=1 bash"
              >
                Copy
              </button>
            </div>
            <p class="install-label">Let Cook desktop · macOS and Linux</p>
            <div class="cmd">
              <code>curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | COOK_INSTALL_DESKTOP_ONLY=1 bash</code>
              <button
                class="copy-btn"
                type="button"
                data-copy
                data-copy-label="Let Cook desktop install command"
                data-copy-text="curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | COOK_INSTALL_DESKTOP_ONLY=1 bash"
              >
                Copy
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cmd" data-windows-cta hidden>
            <span class="cmd-text">
              On Windows, download the Cook CLI or choose the Let Cook desktop installer below.
            </span>
            <a class="copy-btn" data-asset="cli" href="https://download.letcook.dev/cook-1.0.40-windows-x86_64">
              Download CLI
            </a>
          </div>

          <p class="fine">
            Windows users can download the CLI and desktop app below.
            <a href="#install">See all downloads</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="speed">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Fast from the first command</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Cook is a native Rust binary built to start quickly and keep every turn moving.
          </p>
          <ul class="lines">
            <li>
              <strong>Starts in milliseconds.</strong>
              No Node, no Python, no JVM. <code>cook</code> is a single Rust binary on your
              <code>PATH</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Keeps work moving.</strong>
              Streaming, tool calls, and subagents overlap in one runtime instead of waiting in a
              queue.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>A lightweight desktop app.</strong>
              Let Cook uses Tauri and the system webview instead of bundling a browser.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="configure">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Make Cook yours</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Set up your models, skills, commands, and permissions with simple files.
          </p>
          <ul class="lines">
            <li><strong>Models.</strong> Connect your preferred provider and use your own API keys.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Skills and commands.</strong> Add reusable instructions and shortcuts without
              changing the code.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Permissions.</strong> Choose what Cook can read, run, and write.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="install">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Get Cook running</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Install only the app you want. Use the commands on macOS or Linux, or choose a Windows
            download below.
          </p>

          <h3>Let Cook desktop app</h3>
          <ul class="downloads">
